'''King Wahwah''' (チワワン伯爵, ''Chiwawan Hakushaku'', '''Count Chiwawan''') is a [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] enemy introduced in the [[:Category:Advent Stages|Advent Stage]] [[N-1 Grand Prix (Deadly)|King Wahwah's Revenge]]. He was added in [[Version 6.7 Update|Version 6.7]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = King Wahwah
|image = E 257.png
|first appearance = [[N-1 Grand Prix (Deadly)|King Wahwah's Revenge]]<br>'''ZL:''' [[Blessings in Sand|Sub-chapter 7 - Blessings in Sand]]
|money drop = 9,999¢ - 39,496¢
}}

==Enemy==
King Wahwah moves slowly, has high health, great standing range and a massive [[Omni Strike]] area. His devastating attack is evenly distributed into three hits, guaranteed to inflict knockback on each, with very short backswing to easily advance. He has many knockbacks himself that makes it easier to regain ground from him but also increases his survivability, and if he's knocked back during his attack but before his 3rd hit, he'll be able to launch extra hits due to how Multi-Hit works. What makes Wahwah a challenge in [[N-1 Grand Prix (Deadly)|N-1 Grand Prix]] and [[Revenge of N-1 (Merciless)|Revenge of N-1]] is that these stages have restrictions, preventing the use of most units.

