==Trivia==
*The name Wahwah is a play on ''chihuahua'', the world's smallest breed of dog.
*Wahwah's Japanese name, Chiwawan (チワワン) is a pun on チワワ ''chiwawa'' (chiahuahua) and ワン ''wan'' (woof).
*Among the first seven [[:Category:Advent Bosses|Advent Bosses]], King Wahwah appears to represent the sin of pride. Despite being implied to envy his younger brother in his English description, pride is still more likely, as [[Hannya]]'s ''[[wikipedia:Hannya|hannya]]'' mask is already a symbol of jealousy. Wahwah's throne and crown both feature the likeness of a chihuahua (the crown's face can more easily be seen in the [[Media:KingWahwahPoster.jpg|event poster]] for [[N-1 Grand Prix (Deadly)|King Wahwah's Revenge]]) - possibly that of Wahwah himself, indicating that he takes pride in his appearance.
*He was mentioned by name in [[Mistress Celeboodle]]'s Japanese description 2 years before he was introduced.
*According to their Japanese descriptions, Mistress Celeboodle and King Wahwah are a [[wikipedia:Manzai|''manzai'']] comedy duo with Mistress Celeboodle as the ''tsukkomi'' (the short-tempered "straight man" who takes things seriously) and King Wahwah as the ''boke'' (the airheaded "funny man" who gets everything wrong).
**In [[Heaven-Defying Fruit]], Mistress Celeboodle and King Wahwah appear together alongside another comedian, [[Oldstrich]].
**[[N-1 Grand Prix (Deadly)|N-1 Grand Prix]] is likely named after the [[wikipedia:M-1 Grand Prix|M-1 Grand Prix]], the most prevalent ''manzai'' competition in Japan. The "N" presumably stands for ''nyan'', meaning "meow", while the "1" sounds like ''wan'', meaning "woof".
**[[Wrath of the Dogelord (Merciless)|Wrath of the Dogelord]]'s Japanese name, King of [[Doge|Wanko]] (キングオブワンコ ''Kingu obu Wanko'', "King of Doggies"), may be a reference to the annual stand-up comedy tournament [[wikipedia:ja:キングオブコント|King of Conte]] (キングオブコント ''Kingu obu Konto'').
*The combined descriptions of King Wahwah, [[Everlord Wanwan]] and Mistress Celeboodle imply that the little brother mentioned in Wahwah's description is Wanwan, which is not only because Wanwan is a variant of Wahwah but also because Mistress Celeboodle's description states that she married a chihuahua reality TV star. Thus, this leads to Wahwah being Mistress Celeboodle's brother-in-law.
**This is confirmed in Wahwah's Japanese description, which included the name of his younger brother Wanwan years before he was added.
*It can be inferred that the two dogs pulling his chariot are a more haggard female [[Dagshund]] and Mistress Celeboodle. Note the bandana worn by the frontmost dog (the bunny ears) and the wig and tufts of hair on the other dog.
*He has the highest money drop of all [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless Enemies]], and the second highest in the game along with [[Mega Cat (Enemy)|Mega Cat]], which are only beaten by [[Unit-13's False Evolution]].
*The enemy ID he uses (257) was unoccupied until [[Version 6.7 Update|Version 6.7]], when he was added to the game, hence why it's so far behind [[Winged Pigge]] (379) and [[Mystic Mask Yulala]] (380), the other enemies from the same update.

